Subject: [PATCH] observe: write the always-on logs where an iOS app can

The failure channel and the draw log are opened at /tmp/reims-vgpu-*.log.
Inside an iOS app's sandbox /tmp is not writable, the open fails, and every
line is dropped — a refused shader or pipeline, exactly what would explain a
guest that presents frames the device shows black, says nothing at all.

On iOS the process's own temporary directory is used instead
(std::env::temp_dir(), which is what TMPDIR names there); the embedding app
copies the file out where a person can reach it. Every other platform keeps
/tmp, so nothing changes for the pathways in the Supported table, and test
builds keep their per-process files. Which directory a build uses is a fact of
the platform it was compiled for, so it is a target_os cfg and not a switch.

---
diff --git a/crates/reims-vgpu-observe/src/sink.rs b/crates/reims-vgpu-observe/src/sink.rs
index c1b5196b..5bb7e484 100644
--- a/crates/reims-vgpu-observe/src/sink.rs
+++ b/crates/reims-vgpu-observe/src/sink.rs
@@ -112,18 +112,37 @@ fn test_path(kind: &str) -> String {
     format!("/tmp/reims-vgpu-{kind}-test-{}.log", std::process::id())
 }
 
+/// Where a product build's sink of this kind lives.
+///
+/// `/tmp` everywhere but iOS, where an app's sandbox cannot write it: the
+/// open fails, and every line on the always-on failure channel is dropped with
+/// nothing to say so. There the process's own temporary directory is used — on
+/// iOS that is what `TMPDIR` names, and the embedding app copies the file out
+/// to where a person can reach it. Which directory this build uses is a fact
+/// about the platform it was compiled for, not a switch.
+#[cfg(not(any(test, feature = "testing")))]
+fn product_path(kind: &str) -> String {
+    #[cfg(target_os = "ios")]
+    return std::env::temp_dir()
+        .join(format!("reims-vgpu-{kind}.log"))
+        .to_string_lossy()
+        .into_owned();
+    #[cfg(not(target_os = "ios"))]
+    format!("/tmp/reims-vgpu-{kind}.log")
+}
+
 pub fn fail_log_path() -> &'static str {
     #[cfg(any(test, feature = "testing"))]
     return FAIL_PATH.get_or_init(|| test_path("fail"));
     #[cfg(not(any(test, feature = "testing")))]
-    FAIL_PATH.get_or_init(|| "/tmp/reims-vgpu-fail.log".to_string())
+    FAIL_PATH.get_or_init(|| product_path("fail"))
 }
 
 pub fn draw_log_path() -> &'static str {
     #[cfg(any(test, feature = "testing"))]
     return DRAW_PATH.get_or_init(|| test_path("draw"));
     #[cfg(not(any(test, feature = "testing")))]
-    DRAW_PATH.get_or_init(|| "/tmp/reims-vgpu-draw.log".to_string())
+    DRAW_PATH.get_or_init(|| product_path("draw"))
 }
 
